From b422fbe7e3f2f958d70df28ffc8c501720106338 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: newjordan <newjordan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 00:06:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] sycl: extend MoE reorder to Q6_K mul_mat_id; allow
 graph-safe MUL_MAT_ID under SYCL graphs

Q6_K MoE expert weights (e.g. ffn_down_exps in Q4_K_M/Q5_K_M mixes) now get the
per-expert SoA reorder + fused reordered MMVQ, reusing the existing dense Q6_K
reorder traits/readers (dense mmvq, DMMV, dequant GEMM all already reorder-aware).

NX2 B70 ctx0 decode: Q5_K_M 81.1 -> 85.8 t/s (+5.9%), Q4_K_M 85.7 -> 91.0 (+6.2%).
MUL_MAT_ID op tests 690/690 vs CPU; PPL spot check unchanged (5.5723+/-0.153 vs
5.5643+/-0.152).

Also: check_graph_compatibility now admits MUL_MAT_ID nodes that take the fused
no-host-sync TG path (ids stay on device; lazy reorder must already have run).
SYCL graphs stay default-off: on B70 (L0 1.15) per-token graph update throws
'different topology' and re-finalize collapses decode to 15.5 t/s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
